+## Financial baseline and qualification
+
+Active ceiling: **$40 USD per Asia/Dhaka calendar month**, total owner cash authority. V14 reference: ~$24.000000 qualified host class + $0.017182 capped backup/storage/download sensitivity + $6.598836 conservative initial three-minute provider reservation + $9.383982 required cash-coverage capacity = $40.000000. These are conditional planning amounts, not bills, vendor selection, allowance allocation or frozen production caps. Supported taxes/fees/FX, unavoidable extras, safety reserve, existing charges/holds/liabilities must fit before paid commitment; UNKNOWN coverage blocks it.
+
+Every enabled paid operation needs finite complete exposure/reservation and persisted finite attempts; unsupported bounds fail closed. Project/creator authority cannot exceed shared authority, credits cannot override USD, paid failure counts actual owner spending, invalid output never becomes selectable, delivered valid/history output counts applicable allowance once. No free quota assumption. Expected costs/failure rates remain calibration, not the basis for hard safety.
+
+Product duration and financial admission are separate. Three-minute useful reference is conservatively plausible; five-minute alternative leaves $6.041646 cash capacity. Ten-minute full-cap fallback exceeds nominal fixed/provider envelope by $2.314194 before coverage; block/replan or separately admit sufficient verified funding. Initial one-attempt reservation never grants all three policy-permitted attempts automatically. Topic estimates ~12 images/minute; known scripts use reviewed deterministic sentences and actual B groups. Expanded scope recalculates/reauthorizes while consumed work remains recorded. No universal image density or final credit formula is frozen.
+
+## UX, entitlement and acceptance
+
+Warm Creator: warm cream/forest/olive creation, near-black subtle plum/warm-text focused workspace; Light/Dark/System, restrained purposeful motion, accessibility/reduced motion. Composer-first “Tell us what you want to make.” / “We’ll handle the visuals, narration and captions.” See more progressively reveals options. Explicit topic/script choice; paste opens options but does not select mode. Create Video grants bounded authority directly; estimates show credits AND USD in compact/optional Details without mandatory review. Content-scope/translation/adaptation/compound-restore approvals remain explicit.
+
+Desktop left scenes/center selected preview/right Narration or Visual corrections; mobile stacked preview/active correction, scene chooser and secondary sheets, explicit reorder/time controls. All meaningful corrections/status/cancel/render/download remain accessible. Outdated/review/failed/history states and safe next actions are distinct. Simple path auto-renders initial ready production; optional manual review pauses; later corrections do not silently regenerate/rerender.
+
+Canonical [entitlement matrix](../ALPHA_PRODUCT_SPEC.md#owner-decision--research-entitlement-and-topic-discovery-2026-10-05): Research/Topic Suggestions/Custom Suggestions only 3/week and 1/day, Expert only 1/day. Lower tier gets none. Feature eligibility is independent from financial authorization and Alpha allowance promises. Stored random suggestions need no per-click LLM; Custom uses owner model `gemini-3.8-flash`; Expert channel/niche model/permitted retrieval remain unresolved/bounded, never implicit arbitrary URL inspection.
+
+[Invitation gate](../VALIDATION_PLAN.md): ten real English landscape projects spanning topic/pasted 3–10 minutes, ≥8 publishable after ≤15 minutes active corrections each; reliability/selective preservation/isolation/allowance enforcement and operational backup prerequisites also demonstrated. S9 PASS does not establish this gate. Experimental Spanish/French/Bangla/Hindi require narration/caption/export checks before enablement; S6 shaping alone does not prove their publishability. Calibration captures actual costs/billing, failure/retry/regeneration/corrections, text/TTS/sentence counts, storage/render/traffic/unknown outcomes and quality, informing later allowances/credits/pricing.
